Z||000000||87 Sport Coupe||06-25-2001||02:36 AM||||Ok I forgot to put that in the last post but the computer in my 87 Tech 4 Dis is out of a 1985 Pontiac Grand Am it was like this when I got it... I know it out of that because it says 85 grand-am in the yellow like you see from the junk yards... Ok I have no clue as to if they changed my chip-or what ever thing should have been changed over from my Fiero how can I tell? Could this be why I get a Vss code and my service soon light comes on????<BR>Thanks||||reg||4
Z||000001||fieroluke||06-25-2001||03:36 AM||||Hi,<P>yes, that can very well be the case.<BR>The Fiero speedo signal comes from the VSS, goes to the speedo (which divides the frequency by two), and the speedo provides a signal to the ECM. On other GM vehicles (possibly the GrandAm as well) the VSS sensor goes to the ECM, the ECM buffers the signal and feeds it to the IP cluster. To make matters worse, GM used two different VSS generators (magnetic and optical) which generate different frequencies/numbers of pulses per mile. <BR>Even if you have the correct ECM but the wrong PROM, you may confuse the ECM if it thinks you're going 300 in first gear...<P>So, let us know what part number ECM you have<BR>(it should be #1227748), and what PROM is in there. You probably just need a new PROM if you're lucky.<P>Best regards,<BR>-Oliver<P><P>------------------<BR>Visit my website: <A HREF="http://www.fieros.de" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.de</A>  for lots of technical and other Fiero related information<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fieros.de/jpg/mycars.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-25-2001||08:59 PM||||unless someone changed a heck of alot of wire, you can't put a ECM from a non DIS motor in a DIS fiero. Unless Grand Am started DIS in 85, which I don't think it did, then some one marked it wrong.<P>The Grand Am proms I've seen will not work in unmodified fiero without logging VSS error in the ECM. Grand Am feeds VSS to the ECM direct and Fiero feeds it from the dash brains like all other Fiero.<P>There is a workaround for the VSS but I'll have to dig up the data. I don't have it right now. It has the part # to obtain the terminals for the ECM connectors. You can also chop spare connectors from a junk Grand Am or Olds Cutlass Calais (87 or later) and use terminals from them. The ECM is under the pasengers side of the dash in those cars. <P>I do not know if the Olds Cultass PROM will work... I haven't tested the one I have. I'll try to do that in the next few days.<P>The main thing effected by the VSS is that cruise control will not work. I didn't notice any performance problem caused but that doesn't mean there are none. I just didn't run that PROM for more than a day w/o VSS. ||||reg||1
